WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.960
Jay and Silent Bob are coming back to spoof
comic book movies, Hollywood, and more once

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.960
again in Jay and Silent Bob Reboot.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.220
But what if Jason Mewes' and Kevin Smith's
iconic stoner duo did more than just smoke

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.880
herb and spoof superheroes?

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.720
What if they actually went out and joined
the superheroes' world?

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.699
It's not as strange as it might sound.

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:22.670
Kevin Smith has directed and appeared on episodes
of the CW's Arrowverse franchise, and Mewes

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.560
has made appearances on the shows as well.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.460
The duo have also long lent their likenesses
to the Red Bank, New Jersey comic book store

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.340
Jay and Silent Bob's Secret Stash, owned by
Smith since the late '90s.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.860
You may recognize it as the setting of AMC's
Comic Book Men, also developed and produced

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.720
by Smith.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.340
Long before the Arrowverse or the Marvel Cinematic
Universe, Smith's own View Askewniverse beat

00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:47.161
Marvel Studios to the shared universe concept
by an entire decade, with Jay and Silent Bob

00:00:47.161 --> 00:00:49.840
being the main thread tying together many
different movies.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.460
Smith's films have even had comic book tie-ins,
and Jay and Silent Bob have in-universe comic

00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:58.980
book alter egos: Bluntman and Chronic, both
of whom are making a return in the story of

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.380
Jay and Silent Bob Reboot.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.200
So, Jay and Silent Bob have comic book bona
fides, that's been long established.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.000
But what would it look like if Bluntman and
Chronic joined a slightly more serious superhero

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.760
universe?

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.740
What if they suddenly jumped from the Askewniverse
to something a little more fantastical?

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.660
We spoke with Jason Mewes about that possibility
during promotion for his new movie and directorial

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.160
debut, Madness in the Method.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.400
During our chat, we got to talking about the
sweeping next phase of the MCU, which will

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:28.320
include the animated Disney+ series What If…?,
a take on the classic series of speculative

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.420
Marvel comic books.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:34.040
Considering that Marvel Comics has in the
past crossed over with the likes of Star Trek,

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.560
Transformers, and Ash from Evil Dead, it's
not such a weird thing to wonder: what if

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.560
Jay and Silent Bob went out and joined the
MCU?

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.400
If anyone knows the answer, it's Jason Mewes,
a lifelong comic book fan.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.540
And while he may be sober these days, he knows
his on-screen stoner character inside and

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.040
out.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:56.880
"I feel like Jay and Bob would be, like, Bruce
Wayne and Dick Grayson of Earth-14, and then

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.659
we'd turn into Bluntman and Chronic.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.920
So it could almost be like a What If…?"

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:05.039
Mewes imagined the characters' origin story
as being something straight out of Batman

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.620
Begins, which is DC-branded, sure, but we
don't think anyone's going to sue.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:14.540
"Instead of finding the Batcave, and the bats
give Bruce Wayne the idea to dress as a scary

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.490
bat...Jay and Bob going into a cave, and a
bunch of weed is in there.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:23.160
And then all of a sudden we're like, 'There's
the idea, we'll scare everyone with our Chronic

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.080
and Bluntman.'"

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.120
In other words, move over, Moon Knight.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.680
This dynamic duo would make for a much more
amusing take on Batman-style crime-fighting.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.080
Maybe they can cross over at the same time
as Deadpool.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.220
"Yeah it's me, Deadpool, and I've got an offer
that you can't refuse!"

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.060
Of course, there's more than one way to join
the MCU.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.400
Technically speaking, Mewes already exists
in the Marvel movie world, as do Jay and Silent

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:44.940
Bob.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:48.900
That's all thanks to the late Stan Lee, who
made one of his last on-screen appearances

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.520
in 2019's Captain Marvel.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.340
Set in the 1990s, the movie shows Lee reading
the script for Kevin Smith's Mallrats while

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.300
sitting on a train, memorizing his lines out
loud to himself.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.780
Lee also previously made a cameo appearance
in that movie, Smith's second, featured in

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.940
the cast alongside Jay and Silent Bob.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.020
"They look happy, don't they?"

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.440
"What, the bras?"

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.020
But enough of this in-universe speculation,
let's just get direct about it.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.740
Jason Mewes is a working actor, so are there
any comic book characters out there he'd want

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.560
to play?

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.799
The answer is, well, yes, not that he would
necessarily accept the offer to play them.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:26.340
"I think Vigilante or Deadshot would be really
cool to play, 'cause they're two of my favorite

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.640
DC characters.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:34.080
But I don't think I'd want to play a character,
because I love watching the movies, the TV

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.400
shows so much."

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:40.220
Mewes appears to feel this way in general,
not seeming to want to join in on the things

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.110
he enjoys experiencing as a fan.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.900
"I feel like it would throw me out of the
universe if I'm sitting and watching, you

00:03:47.909 --> 00:03:54.299
know, Netflix's Daredevil, and I was playing,
you know, one of the main characters.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.300
Even if it was Froggy Nelson."

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:01.180
He probably means "Foggy Nelson," but give
the guy some credit: "Froggy Nelson" is a

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.860
real character, so long as you're reading
about Deerdevil, and not Daredevil.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:12.000
"I just feel like I wouldn't be able to sit
and enjoy watching it and really getting into

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.080
the stuff if I was a main, main character.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:20.080
But of course I'd love to be in any of the
movies, TV shows, if I was like 'Journalist

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:26.440
#2' who, you know, got to interview them one
or two scenes out of the series, or once in

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.560
the movie or something."

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.960
He doesn't just talk the talk on this topic,
either.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.000
This is more or less exactly what he's done
on the Arrowverse series The Flash, on which

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.660
he's played two characters: "Humvee Guy" and
"Jay the Security Guard."

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.820
"That's my mom's car!"

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.320
So, while you might not see Mewes headlining
a superhero show on DC Universe or Disney+,

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.520
you can definitely catch him making hay on
his home turf as Jay and his alter ego: the

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.520
OG Chronic.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:58.140
You can see Jay and Silent Bob team up again
in Jay and Silent Bob Reboot's touring roadshow,

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.720
kicking off on October 15.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:04.080
And you can also check out Mewes' reunion
with Stan Lee in Madness in the Method.

